<spell-notebook "statistic usage">
	<header level="1">
		Statistic
		<header>A statistic emphasizes the current value of an attribute.</>
	</>
	<statistic-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#events">Events</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  from the old Astro page (Behaviour, Accessibility), tightened. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			A statistic is a value over a label. Write it with the `value` and `label` shorthands, or slot the generic
			`<ui-value>` and `<ui-label>` content parts: inside a statistic they take its look (size, colour, horizontal,
			inverted), so there is no separate statistic-label tag.

			- Slotted parts keep their order: a `<ui-label>` before the `<ui-value>` is Fomantic's top label.
			- The `value` shorthand always comes before the slotted parts and the `label` shorthand after, so either shorthand
			  pairs with a slotted part.
			- A word value is `<ui-value text>` (or `text` with the `value` shorthand): smaller, bold, at least two lines tall.
			- A `<ui-statistics>` group shares its `size`, `color`, `direction` and `inverted` with every statistic in it; a
			  statistic's own attribute still wins.
			- `widths="N"` divides each row of a group evenly (Fomantic's `four statistics`).
			- `stackable` answers to the group's own width, not the window's, so a group in a narrow sidebar stacks even on a
			  wide screen.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-statistics widths="3" size="small">
			  <ui-statistic value="22" label="Faves"></ui-statistic>
			  <ui-statistic color="green" label="Flights">
			    <ui-value><ui-icon name="plane"></ui-icon> 5</ui-value>
			  </ui-statistic>
			  <ui-statistic label="Signups"><ui-value text>Three<br />Thousand</ui-value></ui-statistic>
			</ui-statistics>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Events">
		<markdown>
			Statistics have no events. To update one, set its `value` (or the text of its `<ui-value>`).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			const downloads = document.querySelector("ui-statistic#downloads")
			downloads.setAttribute("value", count.toLocaleString())
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>A statistic is text: it is never a tab stop and takes no keys.</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- A statistic is plain text with no role: it reads as its value, then its label. Name a group of statistics where
			  it matters, with a heading before it or an `aria-label` on a region around it.
			- Write numbers the way they should be read: a screen reader says "5,550", not the size or colour around it.
			- An icon inside a value is decorative unless given a `label`; an image needs its own `alt` (empty when the label
			  already says it all).
			- `color` is never the only signal: say what a red or green value means in the label.
			- If the element fails to render, it shows its slotted `<ui-value>` and `<ui-label>` parts through a
			  bare `<slot>`; the `value` and `label` shorthands, the statistic's look and the spacing between
			  neighbouring statistics go.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
